y is perfect, and his calmness and decision quality are top. B's reliability is not explicitly stated, but \"very conscientious\" suggests reliability but not as strong as 100% reliability. Also B's stress handling is good. C's stress resilience is \"keeps calm in crisis\". Both good.\n\nGiven the panel hasn't discussed A, but we still need to cover all candidates before final. However we need to give a recommendation now. We could propose that we need more info on A before final, but we must give a provisional recommendation. We could say we still vote B, but we need to discuss A. Or we could shift to C. Let's decide to keep B, as we previously argued that memory issue can be mitigated with checklists, while C's egocentric attitude may be harder to mitigate. Also B's stress handling is proven, while C's stress resilience is only \"keeps calm in crisis\" but not proven for ongoing stress. So we keep B.\n\nThus we will produce a public message: we agree with Agent 1's earlier stance, we still recommend B, referencing the arguments. Provide evidence: very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, but note memory issue can be mitigated, communication issues can be addressed. Also note that C's egocentric attitude and lack of further education are more concerning for crew cooperation and adaptability. D's temperament is also severe. So B remains best.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
